{"id": "EUVD-2026-103734", "enisaUuid": "cbf4970e-4bb6-398c-93b7-ea7e84fc8f5d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: atl1: fix soft lockup on out-of-range cmb_tpd_next_to_clean read\n\nSame issue as atl1c (see the first commit in this series, \"net:\natl1c: fix soft lockup on out-of-range tpd_cons read\"): the hardware\ncan report an out-of-range cmb_tpd_next_to_clean (seen as 0xffff)\nwhile the PCIe link/MAC is resetting. An out-of-range value can\nnever be reached and the loop below would spin forever. Treat it as\n\"nothing new to clean\" instead.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d7ac337d37cb97d77e4c910d37746694b606661", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c55e51d5899e80f9593b26985ed0b89e0c828a5e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ab9f61ca851f02ae4398cebaf00735a22e1d6ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/632cd7b81cb7bab36112f02eb2ee7f7cc1214fb1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79e2447b11322c27ef9ac423be0a94efc7691f02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f573b0576252d44fb27ab8470ea873bc6408ef3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6285919d4c06254d257d24dc980f6332e1984a82", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43e746821f5f5afbbf68e388bf9fbe221e03bfca"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98494", "GHSA-9q2h-qvmx-46mv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ea63bb9-4e80-3db1-914d-cf2eaa4421a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "3aad8f06-b2c5-39e8-9f23-f0347bad61a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "3d8323b3-ced5-3362-9cc6-9a66f2f22e27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "4352e99d-f37a-31cb-9eba-5161cce5ee64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "p